note """
The INVERSION of what used to be refusal member 3. A dotted `use` named a flow in
another module and was refused by design; the ruling has the assembler resolve
one through the loader's Packages.ResolveFlow and bind the resolved flow's
outputs BY NAME, exactly as a local `use` already does.

The consumer reaches the upstream module by a go.mod replace, so this fixture
needs no network and no module cache. Its `import` serves only the flow
reference: no Go name in this file is qualified with it, which is why the
generated file must NOT carry that import.
"""
import "example.com/upstream"

flow main
source ingest Feed()
use s upstream.Screen from ingest -> ok, bad
sink emit Report from ok
sink audit Audit from bad
